   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Established Project Steering Committee, Green Agenda Working Group and Technical Advisory Body(s)2. Number of Green Agenda pillar specific Roadmaps developed 3. National Environmental Strategy: Green Agenda for Serbia drafted, and at least 1regulatory act improved on air quality4. Number of IPPC/IED operators supported and trained to prepare IPPC permit applications5.Number of low-carbon development strategies for local self-governments developed6.Number of local waste management plans improved with circular economy requirements7. Number of pilot forest landscape restoration plans developed 8. Number of representatives of LSGs trained on development of air quality plans 9. Number of Innovation Challenge Calls 10. Number of prepared bankable projects in clean technologies for industries 11. Number of identified and elaborated projects for increasing waste collection and recycling rates 12. Number of feasibility studies; 13. Number of workshops organized; 14. Number of annual consultation event with IFIs organized</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. &#x2018;&#x2019;Limited progress&#x2019;&#x2019; reported for Chapters15 and 27 for 2020, lack of coordination of actions 2. Incomplete pillar-specific strategic framework for implementation of the Green Agenda 3. Inappropriate overarching framework for implementation of the Green Agenda  4. No data on dedicated capacity building events for IPPC/IED operators 5. Weak capacities for low-carbon development on the local level 6. No data on implementation of circular economy elements in local waste management plans 7. Low capacities for developing forest landscape restoration plans  8. Insufficient number of innovative solutions and/or business models contributing to GHG emissions reduction. 9. No data on effective governmental procedures to support innovative solutions 10. Insufficient number of prepared bankable projects in clean technologies for industries 11.Insufficient number of identified and elaborated projects for increasing waste collection and recycling rates  12. Low capacities for development of feasibility studies  13. No data on dedicated awareness raising and capacity building events 14. No data on dedicated consultation event with IFIs</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
